{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Divide common marine pollutants into two categories, and provide examples to illustrate.", "output": "Ocean pollutants are divided into organic pollutants and inorganic pollutants. Organic pollutants include petroleum, detergents, and organic chemicals, which can have detrimental effects on aquatic life, such as malnutrition in fish, reproductive issues, and damage to the nervous system. Inorganic pollutants include heavy metals, nitrogen, phosphorus, and oxygenators, which may lead to a reduction in the lifespan of particulates, silt, and organisms in the water environment and may also pose a threat to human health."}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Categorize the waves in the ocean and describe their characteristics respectively.", "output": "Waves in the ocean can be divided into several types, such as surface waves, internal waves, and boundary waves. Surface waves have shorter wavelengths and faster wave speeds, and are often encountered during sea navigation; internal waves are mostly distributed at deeper levels with longer wavelengths, mainly caused by factors such as temperature gradients and salinity gradients; boundary waves are fluctuations generated between the sea bottom sediment layer and the seawater layer."}
