{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Provide a brief introduction to the main elements and compounds found in seawater.", "output": "The primary elements contained in seawater include chlorine, sodium, magnesium, calcium, potassium, sulfur, etc. It also contains various organic compounds, inorganic compounds and the like, such as bromides, phosphates, silicates, etc. These substances affect the balance of the marine ecosystem and the life activities of various organisms."}{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Describe the process and reasons for the formation of ocean currents.", "output": "Ocean currents are formed under the influence of factors such as air currents, gravity, and seabed topography. Among them, air currents are the main driving force, and the Earth's rotational deflection force and geographical topography of the ocean can also affect the formation of ocean currents."}
{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Investigating how waves influence the morphological evolution of coastlines.", "output": "The erosive and depositional processes of ocean waves can alter the shape and geological features of coastlines, over long periods of time create phenomena such as beaches, capes, wave-cut platforms, and cliffs."}
