{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Why is the water temperature near the equator higher?", "output": "Near the equator, the long duration of sunlight and intense ultraviolet rays cause the surface water temperature to rise; at the same time, phenomena such as thermal upwelling also increase the water temperature."}{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "How to avoid the impact of ocean acidification?", "output": "The methods to avoid ocean acidification include: reducing the use of fossil fuels, promoting the development of renewable energy; controlling pollutants emitted from human activities such as industry, agriculture, and animal husbandry; adopting ocean alkalinization technology to increase the carbonate content in seawater."}
