{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "List three commonly used engineering materials in marine construction.", "output": "1. Rebar, 2. Concrete, 3. Aluminum Alloy, 4. Fiberglass, etc."}{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "List several modern marine monitoring technologies, and discuss their respective advantages and disadvantages.", "output": "Modern marine monitoring technologies mainly include satellite remote sensing, marine buoys, drones, and submersibles. Satellite remote sensing has the advantage of large-scale and high spatio-temporal resolution, but has limited sample collection. Marine buoys offer convenient sampling, but the examples are limited. Drone sampling covers a wide range, but it is related to meteorological conditions. While the sampling environment for submersibles is complex, the quality of samples collected is high."}
{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Discuss how to improve the marine environment.", "output": "Improving the marine environment requires various efforts. Firstly, it is necessary to enforce marine environmental protection policies and regulations; secondly, raising public environmental awareness and reducing marine pollution behaviors should be prioritized; furthermore, promoting environmentally friendly technologies, such as marine garbage cleanup, and water pollution management, is essential. In conclusion, only through collective endeavor can we appropriately protect the beautiful marine environment."}
